Diagnosis: two things blocked us. (1) The facts list never contains **any** wine-bottle fact (not even at the start), so `scene.holds("on", wine_bottle_1, …)` can never be true — my bottle success check was impossible. I'll check the bottle *geometrically* instead (near the rack xy and lifted off the table). (2) The descent toward the rack stalls ~8 cm short (a hard blocker — likely the rack body), so a tight `TOL` makes the move "fail" even though the gripper is right at the rack. I'll loosen the place tolerance so the reachable position counts as success, then release. Stove stays last (cold during nearby motion).

